@startuml
title Kaiwa Voice Agent PoC v0.1 — realtime + delayed coaching

autonumber
hide footbox
skinparam ParticipantPadding 16
skinparam BoxPadding 8
skinparam SequenceMessageAlign center
skinparam responseMessageBelowArrow true

actor "Người học\n(Human User)" as U
boundary "Pipecat Web Client\n/browser" as WEB

box "Pipecat realtime process"
  control "SmallWebRTC\nTransport" as RTC
  control "Silero VAD +\nTurn Aggregator" as TURN
  participant "Soniox STT\nstt-rt-v5" as STT
  control "User Turn\nRecorder" as UR
  participant "Kaiwa + Scenario LLM\nOpenAI-compatible" as LLM
  control "Assistant Turn\nRecorder" as AR
  participant "Soniox TTS\ntts-rt-v2" as TTS
end box

collections "Scenario Catalog\npublic/private role data" as CAT
database "SQLite\nsession, turns, report, profile" as DB
participant "Language Coach LLM\nbackground after disconnect" as COACH

note over U,CAT
Human User is an actor, not another LLM agent.
User Role Card contains only public information.
AI hidden facts/events never go to the user card.
end note

== 1. Initialize the session ==

LLM -> CAT: load(scenarioId from environment)
CAT --> LLM: ScenarioSpec(user role, AI role,\nhidden facts/events, success conditions)
LLM -> DB: read LearnerProfile(userId)
DB --> LLM: level, completed sessions, recurring issues
LLM -> DB: create active Session(sessionId)

U -> WEB: Open /client and allow microphone
WEB -> RTC: WebRTC offer + audio track
RTC --> WEB: WebRTC answer + bot audio track

LLM -> LLM: Build private system prompt from\nScenarioSpec + LearnerProfile
LLM -> TTS: Opening Japanese turn
TTS -> RTC: PCM audio chunks
RTC -> WEB: Stream opening audio
WEB -> U: AI opens the role-play naturally

== 2. Realtime conversation loop ==

loop Until the learner disconnects
  U -> WEB: Speak Japanese
  WEB -> RTC: Stream microphone audio
  RTC -> TURN: PCM audio frames

  alt Learner speaks while bot audio is playing
    TURN -> TTS: InterruptionFrame / cancel pending audio
    TURN -> LLM: Cancel the interrupted response
    AR -> AR: Discard incomplete assistant buffer
  end

  TURN -> STT: Speech frames + local endpoint
  STT --> WEB: Interim transcript frames
  STT --> UR: Final TranscriptionFrame
  UR -> UR: Keep final only; deduplicate
  UR -> TURN: Forward transcript
  TURN -> LLM: Context + final learner transcript

  LLM -> LLM: Stay in AI role, respect N-level,\nuse hidden event only when natural
  LLM --> AR: LLM response start + text chunks + end
  AR -> AR: Buffer only complete LLM response
  AR -> TTS: Forward Japanese text chunks
  TTS -> RTC: Stream synthesized PCM
  RTC -> WEB: Bot audio
  WEB -> U: Hear the AI character
  AR -> DB: Turn remains in in-memory session\nuntil finalization
end

== 3. Finalize and coach ==

U -> WEB: Disconnect / finish practice
WEB -> RTC: Close peer connection
RTC -> LLM: on_client_disconnected
LLM -> AR: Discard any incomplete response
LLM -> DB: Save final transcript; state=completed

LLM -> COACH: scenario + transcript evidence
note right of COACH
Coach is a separate context.
It may assess grammar, vocabulary,
politeness, naturalness and task completion.
It must not score pronunciation because
PoC v0.1 has no acoustic metrics.
end note

alt Coach returns valid JSON
  COACH --> LLM: SessionReport JSON
else Coach/API fails
  LLM -> LLM: Create safe rule-based fallback report
end

LLM -> DB: Save report
LLM -> DB: Update completed_sessions + recurring issues
U -> DB: Run report CLI
DB --> U: Latest Vietnamese feedback JSON

== 4. Deferred to phase 2 ==

note over STT,COACH
Not in the realtime critical path:
turn audio -> second-pass ASR -> final transcript
-> forced alignment -> acoustic metrics -> pronunciation feedback.
end note

@enduml

